From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:47:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/30] strip: reduce the LicheeRV Nano-e BSP to a headless
 router base

RNSBox is a headless USB-tethered Reticulum router: no display, camera,
audio, NPU, codec or touch input. Remove the stock overlay pieces and
on-device self-test scripts for those subsystems, no-op the osdrv and media
middleware module builds (they depend on ION/dma-buf symbols this config does
not build), fix a duplicate ion_carveout_heap_create inline that breaks the
build when ION_CVITEK is selected without ION_CARVEOUT_HEAP, disable the
framebuffer/camera nodes in the board DTS, and zero the multimedia and
coprocessor DRAM carve-outs in memmap.py (~127 MB returned to Linux).
